  "configuration_id": "config_043",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieves 0.5266 acc, while RNA-only with the same encoder (config_045) achieves 0.4849, and image-only (config_026) is very weak at 0.2079. This shows RNA is the dominant signal and the image adds a modest ~4% boost. The RNA encoder (pca_n2000) is a linear, unsupervised projection and may be a bottleneck. Question: Does replacing PCA with a learned encoder (scgpt) improve multimodal performance while holding all other factors (singleprofile, resnet50, concat fusion) constant? config_043 is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, isolating the RNA representation effect. Rationale: Since RNA drives most of the predictive signal, improving its representation is the highest-leverage design choice to test next. A positive result would justify further exploration of learned encoders and multiprofile aggregation; a null result would indicate PCA is already near-optimal and redirect effort toward image encoder or fusion strategy. This is the most informative use of the next budget slot."
}

